      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROGER (8) looks to have found the perfect race for his debut. Has had two trial wins this time in, is drawn to get an economical run and has the services of Willie Pike. CALL ME INVINCIBLE (1) looks the pick of the raced brigade. Is on a quick turnaround after a solid second over 1200m at this track seven days ago. Drawn to enjoy a good run and shapes as a major threat. WIN FOR BUSTER (2) is a nine-start maiden who could only manage to finish sixth after being in the firing line on the bend at his latest appearance over 1400m at Bunbury. Not a heap of depth here, so can run an improved race. WILUNA LASS (4) is back at the races for the first time since April 26. Worth noting she filled a minor placing when returning from a spell last prep over 1000m at this track. Comes here with definite claims. DEVIL DOWN (7) didn't set the world on fire at the trials in preparation for the debut but strikes the right race to make an early impact.",
